              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बाळ (bāḷ) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from bāla, \"young; boy\" (CDIAL 9216). CDIAL lists the Marathi form bāḷ, \"young\", and suggests the Sanskrit word perhaps belongs to a word group that gives several words for \"child\"."
